From: panvk-kbase-android worker <panvk-worker@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH csf-v11 124] panvk: transcode BC1-BC7 textures to ASTC 4x4
Generated-by: LLM

Transcode BCn uploads on the GPU into ASTC 4x4 (16 bytes per 4x4 block),
which Mali samples natively:

  BC1/BC2/BC3/BC7      -> ASTC 4x4 LDR (UNORM / SRGB)
  BC4 UNORM            -> ASTC 4x4 LDR, luminance mode, (X,0,0,1) swizzle
  BC5 UNORM            -> ASTC 4x4 LDR, dual-plane luminance-alpha, (X,W,0,1) swizzle
  BC6H UFLOAT/SFLOAT   -> ASTC 4x4 HDR (CEM 11); negative texels clamp to 0
  BC4/BC5 SNORM        -> R8_SNORM / R8G8_SNORM (ASTC has no signed encoding)

The encoder fits each block along its principal colour axis with a
least-squares endpoint refit and picks the best of several single- and
dual-plane modes, instead of the per-channel min/max box diagonal that
desaturated colours, blurred small UI textures and produced black texels
in BC5 normal maps. biblioklept

Measured on Mali-G615 MC2 against the BC-decoded reference (PSNR, before
-> after): BC1 smooth 14.9 -> 41.8 dB, BC3 two-colour 17.6 -> 32.0 dB,
BC7 22-24 -> 41-42 dB, BC5 15.9 -> 34.1 dB, BC4 43.2 -> 50.9 dB,
BC6H 23.4 -> 54.4 dB (tone-mapped), BC4/BC5 SNORM now exact.

Tested GPU: Mali-G615 MC2 (OPPO CPH2763, MT6878 / Dimensity 7300)
Tested Kbase UAPI: 1.21

